-- title:
--   A product of means as an additive-displacement average
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a finite abelian group, and let $f,g:A\to\mathbb R$. Their independent normalized means satisfy
--   $$
--   (\mathbb E_xf(x))(\mathbb E_yg(y))=\mathbb E_{d\in A}\mathbb E_{x\in A}f(x)g(x+d).
--   $$
--   The change of variables replaces an independent pair of points by a starting point and its additive displacement. No sign or boundedness assumptions on $f$ or $g$ are required.
